<title>POLAND: Gorazdze says flood caused it no harm.</title>
<headline>Gorazdze says flood caused it no harm.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish cement maker Gorazdze SA, currently suspended from bourse trade due to the flooding in southern Poland, said in a statement on Tuesday that its plant had sustained no damage.</p>
<p>&quot;The recent events linked with the high level of waters on the Oder (river) caused no problems in the cycle of production nor caused any material harm,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Polifarb Wroclaw, Rafako, ZEW and the parallel market's Viscoplast also remain suspended due to the flooding.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
